Z||000028||stimpy||04-24-2001||10:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RNGCRSH:<BR><B>Stimpy, <P>Helmet or no helmet Matvichuck was hit illegaly. Weight should have been suspended playoffs or not. I think the league is going to crack down on this topic next season.<P>p.s. you sound as if it would have been an even beter hit if Matvichuck would have just died right there - sick!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>OK, lethal hit was a bad choice of wording. Maybe I missed hoow it was an illegal hit, though. I just saw the highlight and it looked like a legal hit, just like the one that Gary Suter took from Scot Mellanby. That's just playoff hockey. If the guys had their helmets on snugly, they wouldn't have gotten their bells rung as hard. One other thing I wish the league would address is seamless glass. That's gotta be like running into concrete. Just think how the Sharks would have fared if their best powerplay defenseman hadn't been knocked out of the series in the first period of game 1.<P>And no, I would not wish to see any players life or career cut short. Well, possible exception for Belfour. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
